{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 138, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Putting a conv on an empty input-to-output edge adds a whole new learnable path, so it gains more than swapping out an op that already gave a path."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, removing edge 3 leaves the output fed only by edge 4 and risks disconnecting the cell, so the drop is much larger."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting edge 0 costs most when it removes a 3x3 conv (as in experiment 72), compared with removing a skip or 1x1 op."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without edge 4, node 1 reaches the output only through edge 2 and node 2, so a better op on edge 0 helps less (experiments 12, 15 and 19 versus 14 and 18)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling op with a 3x3 conv on the first edge adds the most useful capacity (experiments 17 and 18 are strongly positive)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Turning an existing 3x3 conv into a skip loses capacity (experiment 22 dropped sharply), whereas replacing none or a weak op adds a cheap residual."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 gone, the output depends more on edge 5, so removing edge 5 is more likely to break connectivity."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 5 is absent, node 2 never reaches the output, so removing edge 1 costs nothing and can even help (experiment 79)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping pooling for a 3x3 conv on the internal node-1-to-node-2 edge adds depth and parameters on a major path."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing parameter-free pooling with a learnable 3x3 conv on a direct output edge gains more than replacing a skip or 1x1 op."}], "tok": 18769, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_